\section{Agentic Development Workflow}
\label{sec:workflow}

The velocity required to deliver a production-ready full-stack marketing application within
BuildFest timelines demands an AI-native development paradigm \cite{adaptation2026,
blueprint2026}.

\textbf{Claude Code} (Anthropic) operates as a terminal-native autonomous agent. Provided
a high-level natural language prompt describing the application schema, API routes, and
database connections, it scaffolds the Next.js App Router, connects Neo4j and Firecrawl
layers, and manages git operations autonomously. The Vercel MCP plugin dynamically injects
a knowledge graph of the entire Vercel ecosystem into the agent's context window, catching
deprecated patterns via \texttt{postToolUse} validation hooks and enabling autonomous
deployment commands (\texttt{/vercel-plugin:deploy prod}).

\textbf{Cursor IDE}, an AI-native editor built on VS Code, then takes over for granular
human-in-the-loop refinement: tweaking UI components, perfecting dashboard styling, and
refining complex state logic. This sequential pipeline---Claude Code for broad scaffolding,
Cursor for visual polish---condenses development timelines from months to hours.

% ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
\section{Business Model and Commercialisation Strategy}
\label{sec:business}

The engineering architecture described in the preceding sections must be underpinned by
a viable, scalable commercialisation strategy. This section synthesises market research
on competitive pricing, infrastructure economics, distribution mechanics, and emerging
market localisation into a unified business model for the Brand Simulation Engine.

\subsection{Value Proposition and Algorithmic Differentiation}

The platform's core commercial moat is its \textbf{proprietary, multi-engine simulation
stack}. Competing enterprise solutions such as Google Meridian, Meta Robyn, and Recast
either repackage open-source MMM libraries with a modern UI or remain architecturally
confined to single-paradigm regression. The Brand Simulation Engine is the first system
to fuse Bayesian MMM, Agent-Based Modelling, Markov Chain attribution, and NSGA-II
genetic optimisation within a unified GraphRAG backend---delivering causally rigorous,
pre-launch campaign simulation rather than retrospective reporting.

This algorithmic differentiation enables the platform to demonstrably improve client
Return on Ad Spend (ROAS) within 90~days of deployment, transforming the subscription
from a discretionary analytics expense into a revenue-generating investment with a
quantifiable payback period.

\subsection{Revenue Streams and Tiered Pricing Architecture}

The pricing model follows a hybrid B2B SaaS structure designed to capture value across
the full market spectrum:

\begin{table}[H]
  \centering
  \caption{Tiered SaaS Pricing Architecture}
  \label{tab:pricing}
  \renewcommand{\arraystretch}{1.4}
  \begin{tabularx}{\textwidth}{>{\bfseries}p{2.5cm} p{3.0cm} p{3.5cm} X}
    \toprule
    Tier & Target Segment & Monthly Price & Key Inclusions \\
    \midrule
    Starter
      & F-commerce \newline micro-merchants
      & Tk\,1{,}500--2{,}000 \newline(\textasciitilde\$14--18)
      & Single-channel MMM, basic dashboard, Bangla UI, bKash billing \\
    \addlinespace
    Growth
      & SMEs with \newline\$5K--50K ad spend
      & \$99--299/month
      & Multi-channel MMM + ABM, Markov attribution, GraphRAG insights, 5~simulation runs/month \\
    \addlinespace
    Professional
      & Mid-market brands \newline\$50K--500K spend
      & \$499--999/month
      & Unlimited simulations, NSGA-II optimisation, SHAP explainability, white-label reporting \\
    \addlinespace
    Enterprise
      & Brands with \newline\$500K+ spend
      & Custom annual \newline contract
      & Dedicated infrastructure, custom model calibration, API access, unlimited seats, SLA \\
    \bottomrule
  \end{tabularx}
\end{table}

The \textbf{Starter} tier is strategically priced at purchasing-power parity for
Bangladesh, ensuring accessibility for the 300{,}000+ F-commerce merchants operating
on micro-budgets of \$20--50/month. The \textbf{Enterprise} tier employs custom
contracts anchored to the client's aggregate monthly media spend and channel count,
with unlimited user seats to maximise internal adoption and reduce churn.

Expansion revenue is captured through usage-based overages (additional simulation
batches beyond tier limits) and modular add-ons such as promotional depth optimisation
(priced at 25\% of the base subscription) and competitor intelligence feeds.

\subsection{Infrastructure Cost Optimisation}

The business model's gross margin is structurally protected by a \textbf{bifurcated
serverless architecture} that eliminates idle compute costs:

\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
  \item \textbf{CPU-Bound Workloads} (API routing, data ingestion, UI rendering) execute
        on \textbf{AWS Lambda} using ARM (Graviton) processors, achieving up to 36\%
        cost reduction versus x86 configurations. The free tier (1M invocations/month)
        subsidises early-stage operations.
  \item \textbf{GPU-Bound Workloads} (Bayesian inference via PyMC, NSGA-II optimisation
        loops, model training) execute on \textbf{Modal}'s serverless GPU infrastructure,
        which auto-scales from zero and provisions containers in under one second.
        Documented benchmarks demonstrate 12--20\% cost savings versus reserved GPU
        instances for bursty ML workloads.
\end{itemize}

This segregation ensures that expensive GPU compute is consumed only during active
simulation execution and scales to zero between requests, enabling aggressive
low-tier pricing without margin erosion.

\subsection{Go-to-Market: White-Label Agency Distribution}

Direct-to-brand sales cycles for complex analytics SaaS are protracted and
capital-intensive. The primary distribution strategy leverages existing digital
marketing agencies as localised resale channels through a \textbf{white-label
partnership programme}.

Under this model, agencies purchase wholesale access to the platform infrastructure,
completely rebrand the application with their own corporate identity and custom domains,
and resell the service to their end-clients as a proprietary, in-house analytical
advantage. The agency controls the retail pricing, manages the billing relationship,
and provides tier-1 support. The Brand Simulation Engine operates silently in the
background, powering the serverless infrastructure and pushing algorithmic updates.

This structure delivers three compounding advantages:

\begin{enumerate}[leftmargin=*, label=(\roman*)]
  \item \textbf{Capital-efficient scaling.}~The operational burden of localised sales,
        onboarding, and support shifts to agency partners, enabling geographic expansion
        without proportional headcount growth.
  \item \textbf{Sticky revenue.}~Agencies embed the platform into their daily workflows
        and client reporting, transforming the SaaS from a discretionary tool into core
        operational infrastructure with high switching costs.
  \item \textbf{Retail margin arbitrage.}~Agencies purchasing wholesale sub-accounts
        at \$49--99/month retail the dashboard to SMB clients at \$197--497/month,
        generating substantial recurring software revenue that incentivises aggressive
        client acquisition.
\end{enumerate}

\subsection{Emerging Market Penetration: The Bangladesh Playbook}

Bangladesh presents a greenfield opportunity characterised by massive F-commerce volume
(300{,}000+ Facebook-based merchants), rapidly growing digital ad spend, and zero
existing predictive marketing intelligence competitors. The go-to-market strategy for
this market operates across four axes:

\begin{enumerate}[leftmargin=*, label=\textbf{(\arabic*)}]
  \item \textbf{Hyper-Localised Pricing.}~The Starter tier is denominated in BDT and
        priced below the cost of a single agency retainer hour, ensuring that local
        agencies operating on Tk\,10{,}000--50{,}000 monthly client retainers can
        profitably integrate the platform.
  \item \textbf{Payment Infrastructure Integration.}~Direct integration with
        \textbf{bKash Auto Pay} (70M+ active users) enables frictionless automated
        recurring BDT subscription billing, bypassing the high failure rates and
        unavailability of Western payment rails (Stripe, PayPal). Secondary gateway
        support includes \textbf{SSLCommerz}, \textbf{Nagad}, and
        \textbf{Portwallet} for developer-friendly API routing.
  \item \textbf{Institutional Partnerships.}~Strategic alignment with the
        \textbf{e-Commerce Association of Bangladesh (e-CAB)} and the
        \textbf{Bangladesh Association of Software and Information Services (BASIS)}
        provides access to subsidised SME SaaS distribution channels, government
        digitisation initiatives under the ``Smart Bangladesh'' programme, and
        corporate tax exemptions for software companies.
  \item \textbf{Limit Pricing for Entry Deterrence.}~Initial pricing is set
        deliberately below the static monopoly optimum to signal to potential local
        competitors that the sector does not offer easy margins, deterring fast-follower
        entry and protecting long-term market structure.
\end{enumerate}

